## 1. Product Overview

You are building a managed AI employee service. Each client receives a dedicated Mac Mini M4 with a fully configured AI agent that controls the desktop 24/7, communicates over Slack, and handles real business tasks — email, calendar, research, document creation, web browsing, and more.

The product is built on three foundations:

- **OpenClaw (MIT licensed)** — the open-source agent loop, memory system, and skills marketplace
- **Claude Computer Use API** — gives the agent eyes and hands on the Mac desktop
- **Your proprietary layer** — provisioning, billing, dashboard, Slack UX, and support

> **Your Competitive Position:** OpenClaw provides the engine. You provide the car. The managed service, hardware, branding, onboarding, and support are your moat. Your clients never install anything. They open Slack and their AI employee is already there, working.

### 1.1 What the Product Does

The AI employee can perform any task a human VA could do on a computer:

- Read, reply to, and organise Gmail
- Schedule, reschedule, and summarise Google Calendar events
- Research topics on the web and produce written summaries
- Create Google Docs, Sheets, and Slides
- Fill out web forms and navigate websites visually
- Post to Slack channels on behalf of the client
- Run terminal commands and scripts on the Mac
- Execute custom workflows via OpenClaw skills

