### PHASE 0 — Environment Setup

**Duration:** 1 Day · **Difficulty:** Easy

#### 0.1 Mac Mini Initial Configuration

Perform these steps manually on each Mac Mini before running any scripts:

1. System Settings → General → Login Items: Enable auto-login
1. System Settings → Privacy & Security → Accessibility: Grant Terminal full access
1. System Settings → Privacy & Security → Screen Recording: Grant Terminal access
1. Install BetterDummy — create a virtual 1920x1080 display
1. Install Node.js v20+ via homebrew: `brew install node`
1. Install Python 3.11+: `brew install python`
1. Install Chrome and sign into the client Google account
1. Enable Screen Sharing for remote monitoring

#### 0.2 Fork & Clone OpenClaw

Fork OpenClaw on GitHub under your own organisation, then clone:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_ORG/openclaw.git
cd openclaw
npm install
npm run build
```

> ⚠️ **Important — Lock Your Fork:** Immediately after forking, pin your dependencies (`npm shrinkwrap`) and create a production branch. Never auto-merge upstream changes without testing first. OpenClaw is community-maintained — a breaking change could take down all your clients.

