### PHASE 2 — Computer Use Desktop Control

**Duration:** 5–7 Days · **Difficulty:** Hard

This is the most technically complex phase. It transforms the agent from a text chatbot into an agent that can actually see and control the Mac desktop. This is your core differentiator.

#### 2.1 How Computer Use Works

1. Capture a screenshot of the virtual display
1. Send screenshot + task description to Claude Computer Use API
1. Claude returns a list of actions (click, type, scroll, key press)
1. Execute each action via PyAutoGUI
1. Capture a new screenshot and send back to Claude
1. Repeat until Claude signals `task_complete` or max iterations reached

#### 2.2 Safety Guardrails (Critical)

> 🚨 **Build these before going live:**
> 
> - **MAX_ITERATIONS:** Hard cap at 30 screenshot loops per task. Beyond this, kill and report failure.
> - **MAX_COST_PER_TASK:** If a task consumes more than $0.50 in API tokens, terminate it.
> - **CONFIRMATION_REQUIRED:** Before sending any email, deleting any file, or making any purchase, the agent must send a Slack message asking for approval and wait for a “yes” response.
> - **FORBIDDEN_ACTIONS:** Maintain a list of apps/URLs the agent can never open (banking sites, etc.)
> - **SCREENSHOT_LOG:** Save every screenshot taken during a task for 30 days (proof of work + debugging).

#### 2.3 Python Computer Use Controller

Computer Use actions are executed via Python (PyAutoGUI). This runs as a sidecar process:

```bash
pip install pyautogui pillow anthropic
```

```python
# computer_use_controller.py
import pyautogui, anthropic, base64, json
from PIL import ImageGrab

def capture_screen():
    img = ImageGrab.grab()
    img.save("/tmp/screen.png")
    with open("/tmp/screen.png", "rb") as f:
        return base64.b64encode(f.read()).decode()

def execute_action(action):
    if action["type"] == "mouse_move":
        pyautogui.moveTo(action["x"], action["y"])
    elif action["type"] == "left_click":
        pyautogui.click(action["x"], action["y"])
    elif action["type"] == "type":
        pyautogui.typewrite(action["text"], interval=0.02)
    elif action["type"] == "key":
        pyautogui.press(action["key"])
    elif action["type"] == "scroll":
        pyautogui.scroll(action["direction"], action["x"], action["y"])
```

