### PHASE 6 — Provisioning Automation

**Duration:** 2–3 Days · **Difficulty:** Medium

Without automation, setting up each new Mac Mini takes 2–3 hours and is error-prone. This phase builds a script that provisions a fresh Mac Mini in under 20 minutes.

#### 6.1 Provisioning Script Flow

1. Admin fills in onboarding form (client name, Google account, Slack token, plan)
1. Dashboard generates `provision.sh` with all values pre-filled
1. Admin downloads `provision.sh`, copies to Mac Mini, runs it
1. Script installs all dependencies, clones your fork, configures launchd
1. Agent starts, connects to Slack, sends welcome message to client
1. Mac Mini registers itself with your dashboard via heartbeat

#### 6.2 What the Script Does

- Installs Node.js, Python, homebrew, BetterDummy
- Clones your locked fork of OpenClaw
- Writes `persona.json` and `client.json` from the form data
- Creates and loads the launchd plist for auto-start
- Sets up SQLite database with correct schema
- Runs first-boot test — sends a test message to confirm Slack connection
- Sends “Your AI employee Alex is ready!” message to client Slack channel

#### 6.3 Claude Code Prompt — Phase 6

```
"Build a bash script generator in TypeScript. It takes a ClientConfig object (name,
slackToken, googleAccountEmail, plan, agentName, timezone) and outputs a provision.sh
bash script that: (1) installs all dependencies via homebrew and pip, (2) clones the
agent repo from GitHub, (3) writes persona.json and client.json with the provided values,
(4) creates a launchd plist at ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.aiemployee.agent.plist that
starts on login and restarts on crash, (5) runs npm install and npm run build, (6) starts
the agent and verifies it sends a test Slack message. Make the script idempotent so
re-running it is safe."
```

