### PHASE 7 — Billing, Usage Caps & Reporting

**Duration:** 3–4 Days · **Difficulty:** Medium

#### 7.1 Billing Architecture

- Stripe handles monthly subscriptions — one product per plan tier
- Each Mac Mini tracks its own token usage in SQLite
- Every 24 hours, usage is synced to Supabase
- If a client hits their daily task limit, the agent pauses and sends a Slack notification
- If they exceed by 20%, charge overage at $0.05 per task via Stripe metered billing

#### 7.2 Plan Limits

|Limit              |Assistant $997|Pro $1,997      |Executive $3,497        |
|-------------------|--------------|----------------|------------------------|
|Tasks/day          |20            |50              |100                     |
|Computer Use tasks |5/day         |20/day          |50/day                  |
|Max iterations/task|15            |25              |30                      |
|Memory retention   |30 days       |90 days         |Unlimited               |
|Report frequency   |Weekly        |Weekly + Monthly|Daily + Weekly + Monthly|
|Support            |Email (48h)   |Email (24h)     |Slack direct (same day) |

#### 7.3 Weekly Report Contents

Every Monday morning the agent generates and sends a PDF report to the client via Slack:

- Total tasks completed this week
- Breakdown by category (email, calendar, research, documents, web)
- Estimated hours saved (assume 12 min per task)
- Top 5 tasks with screenshots
- API cost (internal — do not show to client)

#### 7.4 Claude Code Prompt — Phase 7

```
"Build a UsageManager class that: (1) increments task counts in SQLite after each task,
(2) checks against plan limits from client.json before starting each task, (3) if at 80%
of daily limit sends a Slack warning, (4) if at 100% pauses the agent and sends a
limit-reached message with an upgrade link, (5) resets counts at midnight client timezone
using node-cron. Also build a WeeklyReport class that queries the past 7 days of tasks
from SQLite, generates a Markdown summary, converts it to PDF using puppeteer, and
uploads it to the client Slack channel."
```

